Check that all components are communicating properly:

Verify Prometheus can scrape all targets:

curl -s http://localhost:9090/api/v1/targets | grep -o '"health":"[^"]*"' | sort | uniq -c
Check Alertmanager connectivity:

curl -s http://localhost:9090/api/v1/alertmanagers
Verify metrics are being collected:

curl -s http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query?query=up | grep -o '"value":\[[^]]*\]'
Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Service fails to start

Check service status: sudo systemctl status [service-name]
View logs: sudo journalctl -u [service-name] -f
Verify file permissions and ownership
Issue 2: Targets showing as down

Verify the service is running on the expected port
Check firewall settings: sudo ufw status
Test connectivity: curl http://localhost:[port]/metrics
Issue 3: Configuration errors

Validate YAML syntax: promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml
Check for indentation issues in YAML files
Verify file paths and permissions
Issue 4: Alerts not firing

Check alert rule syntax: promtool check rules /etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml
Verify evaluation interval in prometheus.yml
Check if conditions are actually met
Issue 5: High resource usage

Monitor Prometheus metrics about itself
Adjust scrape intervals if needed
Check retention settings
Verification Commands
Run these commands to verify your setup:

# Check all services are running
sudo systemctl status prometheus node_exporter process_exporter alertmanager

# Verify all ports are listening
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep -E ':(9090|9100|9256|9093)'

# Test metric collection
curl -s http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query?query=up | jq .

# Check target health
curl -s http://localhost:9090/api/v1/targets | jq '.data.activeTargets[] | {job: .labels.job, health: .health}'
Conclusion
In this lab, you have successfully:

Set up a complete Prometheus monitoring stack on a single Linux machine, including the Prometheus server, Node Exporter, Process Exporter, and Alertmanager
Understood the architecture and how each component plays a specific role in the monitoring ecosystem
Configured exporters to collect system and process metrics, demonstrating how Prometheus gathers data from various sources
Implemented alerting with Alertmanager and created meaningful alert rules for system monitoring
Explored PromQL by writing and executing queries to extract insights from collected metrics
Navigated the Prometheus UI to visualize data, monitor targets, and manage alerts
This hands-on experience demonstrates how Prometheus components work together to create a comprehensive monitoring solution. The Prometheus server acts as the central hub, exporters provide specialized metrics, Alertmanager handles alert routing and notifications, and PromQL enables powerful data analysis. Understanding this architecture is crucial for implementing effective monitoring in production environments.

The skills you've developed in this lab form the foundation for more advanced Prometheus deployments, including service discovery, federation, and integration with visualization tools like Grafana.
